confirm.description:
{changes}

**Apply all** writes these changes to `{folder}` and reloads ZHA: your Zigbee devices are unavailable for a few seconds. If a step fails, xquirks tries to put back what it changed.

**Not now** puts this list aside. A different list comes back as a new repair.

abort.failed_partly:
Stopped at a failure: {failed}

xquirks could not put these changes back:

{left}

ZHA loads what is in `{folder}` now or at its next start. The next list sets the rest right.

held_back.description:
{picture}{devices}

xquirks has `{file}` for it ({status}) but holds it back until it is verified on a device. {reasons}

To get it anyway, turn on **Offer high-risk files** under Settings > Devices & services > xquirks > Configure. The next change list then offers it.

not_applied.description:
{picture}xquirks installed `{file}`, but ZHA does not apply it to these devices:

{devices}

A device on another custom quirk: that file wins. Remove one of the two. A device on no quirk: ZHA could not load the file. See the Home Assistant log.

misfit.description:
{picture}`{file}` does not fit the endpoints of these devices, so xquirks does not install it for them. A device that runs an older version keeps it until an update for other devices replaces it:

{devices}

Each link opens a prefilled report on GitHub with the device's endpoints and clusters, without its name or address. With it, a later version of the file can fit the device.

confirm.description:
Changed since ZHA last loaded `{folder}`:

{changes}

Reload ZHA now? Your Zigbee devices are unavailable for a few seconds. A restart of Home Assistant does the same.

download_waiting.description:
xquirks could not download these files of the change list yet:

{files}

The change list waits until it has checked them. xquirks tries again every 15 minutes.
